# ── Front-end build (Vite) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The multiplayer game server's base URL. WebSocket URLs are derived from it by
# swapping the scheme (https→wss), so this is the ONLY place the server address
# lives. Must be reachable over TLS in production — an https page cannot open a
# ws:// (non-TLS) socket.
#
#   • Local dev:  leave unset. RemoteRoom.serverBase() falls back to
#                 http://localhost:8787 (the `npm run server:dev` wrangler URL).
#   • Production: set this in the Vercel project's Environment Variables to the
#                 deployed Worker URL, then redeploy. A prod build with this
#                 UNSET throws a clear error at connect time instead of silently
#                 dialing localhost. See DEPLOY.md.
#
# VITE_GAME_SERVER=https://mahjong-server.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev

# ── Coach proxy (Vercel serverless functions: api/coach.ts, api/review.ts) ───
# The coach runs SAME-ORIGIN with the front end (relative /api/* URLs), so it
# needs no URL config. It does need the Anthropic key, set as a Vercel env var
# (server-side, NOT prefixed VITE_ — must never reach the browser bundle):
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Worker (Cloudflare) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Worker's own config lives in server/wrangler.jsonc (vars) and in secrets
# set via `wrangler secret put` — NOT in this file. For reference:
#   • ALLOWED_ORIGINS (var)   comma-separated allowlist of front-end origins.
#                             Empty = allow any (dev only). Set in prod.
#   • ADMIN_KEY (secret)      `wrangler secret put ADMIN_KEY` — debug/reset auth.
